{"name":"Wise Owl","hex":"#cdbba5","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wise","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Showing good judgement or the benefit of experience.","Disrespectful."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To become wise.","Usually with \"up\", to inform or learn."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wise"},{"term":"owl","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Old Welsh."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various birds of prey of the order Strigiformes, families Strigidae and Tytonidae, that are primarily nocturnal and have forward-looking, binocular vision, limited eye movement, and good hearing. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A person seen as having owl-like characteristics, especially appearing wise or serious, or being nocturnally active."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/owl"}],"entries":[{"title":"Owl","blocks":[{"text":"Owls are birds from the order Strigiformes, which includes over 200 species of mostly solitary and nocturnal birds of prey typified by an upright stance, a large, broad head, binocular vision, binaural hearing, sharp talons, and feathers adapted for silent flight. Exceptions include the diurnal northern hawk-owl and the gregarious burrowing owl."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Bubo_bubo_sibiricus_-_01.JPG/330px-Bubo_bubo_sibiricus_-_01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Owl","wikidata":"Q25222"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Bubo_bubo_sibiricus_-_01.JPG/500px-Bubo_bubo_sibiricus_-_01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Bubo_bubo_sibiricus_-_01.JPG/1280px-Bubo_bubo_sibiricus_-_01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x